<title>UK: INTERVIEW - British-Borneo moves up a gear.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW - British-Borneo moves up a gear.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>British-Borneo Petroleum Syndicate Plc said on Wednesday moves to raise new capital, treble its number of shares and purchase Gulf of Mexico assets from Conoco signified that it was &quot;moving to a different level of activity&quot;.</p>
<p>Finance director Bill Colvin told Reuters that the oil exploration and production company was now competing for assets with the biggest companies in the world and needed to beef up its balance sheet as a result.</p>
<p>He conceded that the company could be a takeover target but said it had had no approaches.</p>
</text>
